                "entry_id": "86ca8901-c2b7-3fb4-b51d-d3f8d6c80f3e",
                "word": "inédie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c416df48-ce2a-4ad7-b70b-8e2664af87ce",
                        "entry_id": "86ca8901-c2b7-3fb4-b51d-d3f8d6c80f3e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "inédies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1749d003-5e09-3947-b65e-e2f67ecf1c71",
                        "entry_id": "86ca8901-c2b7-3fb4-b51d-d3f8d6c80f3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abstinence absolue et prolongée de toute nourriture et parfois de toute boisson."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Paranormal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c281606-6964-4a61-8848-74795d343229",
                                "sense_id": "1749d003-5e09-3947-b65e-e2f67ecf1c71",
                                "text": "Plus rare, Padre Pio vécut en inédie (abstention totale de nourriture et de boisson) à plusieurs reprises."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6c9a8ea-0656-4fff-9626-0704b819ae8b",
                                "sense_id": "1749d003-5e09-3947-b65e-e2f67ecf1c71",
                                "text": "À partir de 1930, Marthe Robin ne se nourrit plus que de l’hostie consacrée et ne sortira quasiment plus jamais de sa chambre, à Châteauneuf-de-Galaure, sa commune natale où elle est restée toute sa vie. Elle vivra plus de 50 ans dans cette situation d’inédie, le terme médical définissant l’absence d’alimentation. Ses cinq décennies de survie dans cette condition demeurent un mystère médical et un sujet de controverse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03fb3ecf-1439-4734-966e-54d2f57ee652",
                                "sense_id": "1749d003-5e09-3947-b65e-e2f67ecf1c71",
                                "text": "L’inédie est la soit-disante (sic) capacité de vivre sans manger. Certains inédiens subsisteraient par la respiration, comme la Bavaroise Thérèse Neumann (1898-1962), qui en plus de porter des stigmates, disait que « l’on peut subsister avec le souffle divin comme seule nourriture »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60b75b21-1536-45a3-9834-1e0b01fe7b26",
                        "source_entry_id": "86ca8901-c2b7-3fb4-b51d-d3f8d6c80f3e",
                        "source_sense_id": "1749d003-5e09-3947-b65e-e2f67ecf1c71",
                        "target_lang_word": "Nahrungslosigkeit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b11e4fb9-d6cc-4caa-a251-e5eef56bacf8",
                        "source_entry_id": "86ca8901-c2b7-3fb4-b51d-d3f8d6c80f3e",
                        "source_sense_id": "1749d003-5e09-3947-b65e-e2f67ecf1c71",
                        "target_lang_word": "inedia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inedia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79300156-baf1-3fe7-b699-9b8f91ae8077",
                                        "entry_id": "a7c7f79d-6e1d-396e-9f95-e6779041bcf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The (purported) ability to live without food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e67ce23-5628-4c16-b5ed-cdb770fed5a7",
                                                "sense_id": "79300156-baf1-3fe7-b699-9b8f91ae8077",
                                                "text": "The problems of establishing the facts are redoubled when the discussion is narrowed to the type of inedia which in itself is less susceptible to natural explanation and intrinsically more plausible as a sign: active inedia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "358ef9ab-0100-47dd-abbc-2f3e70f324e3",
                                                "sense_id": "79300156-baf1-3fe7-b699-9b8f91ae8077",
                                                "text": "Stigmatics are by no means the only mystics to experience inedia; on the contrary, it is a condition that has been experienced by a great many Catholic mystics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8699400e-aff8-4b26-a0e3-0b6e313a9f0e",
                                                "sense_id": "79300156-baf1-3fe7-b699-9b8f91ae8077",
                                                "text": "Vigorous debates on inedia clearly illustrate the range of difficulties. Unlike visions and locutions, accessible only to those who experience them, inedia can be observed and monitored by others."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
